            <ArticleTitle>[The effect of molsidomine on the conjunctival microcirculation in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sublingual administration of molsidomin in average dose of 3 mg with an interval of 15 and 60 minutes was used in the treatment of 24 patients with ischemic heart disease with stable exertion stenocardia of the II-III functional classes. Course treatment in optimal chosen doses resulted in an improvement of the indices of conjunctival microcirculation and rheological properties of erythrocytes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
